{"seq":9,"trial_id":"gbrain-arm-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-heldout/sc-05-hartford-postmortem/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-24T09:56:11.468Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"b7635284d8ac84570d98cd4b41462cd027b6d7eca8cb42e0fac8e99a5d3960f9","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1MTZS8410N","text":"Gideon, in #inc-vtg-hartford on 3 Aug, your first report of the kiosks offline was at **10:42 AM**. The channel's first message is yours, and it says the gate kiosks were offline at the Hartford plant, with both inbound lanes showing a white screen after badge scan.\n\nFor the guard, the only record is your 10:42 message: \"Guard is writing trailer numbers on a clipboard.\" Nothing else in the channel describes what the guard did. The later messages cover the other side of it:\n\n- **10:44:** Mateo reported six trucks waiting at the east gate.\n- **11:03:** Mateo wrote \"Kiosk 1 is back. Guard checked in trailer 8836; dispatch sees it.\" That is the first record of the guard checking a trailer in on the system after the outage.\n- **11:08:** You wrote that both lanes were working as of 11:07.\n\nSo between 10:42 and 11:03 the guard was logging trailers on paper, and the system check-in resumed at 11:03. If the postmortem needs the guard's own account, it would have to come from them directly, since the channel doesn't have it."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1MTZS8410N","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
